Package: netwtop
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, iproute2, procps
Description: interactive per-user network traffic monitor
 netwtop is a terminal network monitor for Linux and macOS inspired by nvitop.
 It displays authoritative per-interface upload and download rates together
 with best-effort per-user and per-command attribution, rolling history,
 interface switching, and a responsive interactive table.
 .
 The implementation uses POSIX shell, awk, and operating-system counters. On
 Linux, iproute2 ss provides TCP attribution while sysfs provides interface
 totals. Root access is optional and enables command details for other users.
